.TH QWPIPE 1 "November 2026" "Local-LLM-Unsensored" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qwpipe \- process standard input streams with local Qwen3-4B
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I command
|
.B qwpipe
[\fB\-c\fR \fI16\fR|\fI32\fR|\fI48\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fI0..4\fR]
[\fIprompt\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qwpipe
reads arbitrary piped data from standard input (such as shell command outputs, build logs, diffs, network traces, or system journal dumps) and feeds it into the local Qwen3-4B model with user instructions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " tokens"
Set context window size (16, 32, or 48 thousand tokens). Default is 32.
.TP
.BI \-r " level"
Set reasoning effort level (\fI0\fR to \fI4\fR). Default is 2.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Analyze compilation errors from a build log:
.RS
.nf
make 2>&1 | qwpipe "Explain the root cause of the build failure and give a fix"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Analyze a git diff before committing:
.RS
.nf
git diff | qwpipe "Review this patch for bugs and suggest a clean commit message"
.fi
.RE
